{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.counts_affine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.counts_affine","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L253-L260","doc":"Both counts are **affine** in `(Z, N)`: their second differences in `Z`\nvanish. This is what `CrossingCountAffine` needs, now from the construction\nrather than from a fitted formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.strong_channel_mirror_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.strong_channel_mirror_difference","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L247-L251","doc":"**The strong channel is not**: it differs by `4(Z - N)`. The charge\ndependence is present, in the wrong channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.coulomb_channel_mirror_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.coulomb_channel_mirror_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L239-L245","doc":"**The Coulomb channel is mirror-invariant.** Its multiplicity `n₊ + n₋`\ndepends only on `A = Z + N`, so it takes the same value on `(Z, N)` and `(N, Z)`\n— hence contributes exactly zero to every mirror splitting, for every nucleus\nrather than for the five that were checked. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.count_avg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.count_avg","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L235-L237","doc":"**`n_avg = 2A + 1`**, as `atom_braid_word_3A`'s own docstring states. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.count_writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.count_writhe","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L230-L233","doc":"**`n₊ - n₋ = 4Z`** — the writhe, the strong-channel multiplicity, carrying\nall of the charge dependence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.count_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.count_sum","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L225-L228","doc":"**`n₊ + n₋ = 10A - 2`** — the Coulomb-channel multiplicity, depending on `A`\nalone. Proved, not sampled. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.nMinus_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.nMinus_closed","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L221-L223","doc":"`n₋ = 3Z + 5N - 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.nPlus_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.nPlus_closed","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L217-L219","doc":"`n₊ = 7Z + 5N - 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.nAvg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.nAvg","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L213-L215","doc":"Averaged (non-braid) letters: `2` per nucleon, plus the single pn interface —\na chain on `p^Z n^N` has exactly one p→n transition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.nMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.nMinus","kind":"def","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L209-L211","doc":"Negative crossings: `3` per proton, `4` per neutron, plus one per nn\ninterface, of which there are `N - 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.nPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.nPlus","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L205-L207","doc":"Positive crossings: `6` per proton, `5` per neutron, plus one per pp\ninterface, of which a chain on `p^Z n^N` has `Z - 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.complete_count_difference_doubled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.complete_count_difference_doubled","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L189-L193","doc":"**The complete graph's bond-count difference is `(Z-N)(A-1)/2`**, stated\ndoubled: `Z(Z-1) - N(N-1) = (Z-N)(Z+N-1)`. Linear in `A`, which is the `A¹`\nscaling the probe measured. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.chain_count_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.chain_count_difference","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L184-L187","doc":"**The chain assembly's bond-count difference is `Z - N`** — no factor of `A`,\nwhich is the `A⁰` scaling the probe measured. A chain on `p^Z n^N` has `Z-1` pp\nbonds and `N-1` nn bonds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.mirror_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.mirror_difference","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L175-L182","doc":"**The mirror difference is `(n_pp - n_nn)(b_pp - b_nn)`.** Under `p ↔ n` the\npp and nn counts trade and the pn count is fixed, so everything else cancels —\nincluding the pn term entirely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.additiveBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.additiveBinding","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L170-L173","doc":"An additive binding: `n_pp` pp bonds, `n_nn` nn bonds, `n_pn` pn bonds, each\ncontributing its own energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.isovector_over_isoscalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.isovector_over_isoscalar","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L150-L156","doc":"**The isovector term is `2/δ` times the isoscalar one**, in the quadrupled\nnormalisation: `4·(f_pp - f_nn) = (4/δ)·(T01 splitting)`, i.e. the ratio is a\nfact about `δ` alone and carries no other structure. Stated division-free as the\ncross-multiplied identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.bring_T01_quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.bring_T01_quad","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L144-L148","doc":"**`bring_color_weighted`'s `T = 0` / `T = 1` splitting is exactly `hδ/4`**,\nstated quadrupled as `hδ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.strict_T01_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.strict_T01_zero","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L138-L142","doc":"**`strict_averaged` puts `f_pn` exactly on the like-pair midpoint**, so its\n`T = 0` / `T = 1` splitting is identically zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.like_pair_even_doubled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.like_pair_even_doubled","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L132-L136","doc":"The charge-**even** part of the like-pair channel, doubled: `f_pp + f_nn =\n2z - h`. Together with `fPP_sub_fNN` this is the full parity decomposition —\neven `= z - h/2`, odd `= h/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.fPP_sub_fNN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.fPP_sub_fNN","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L126-L130","doc":"**`f_pp - f_nn = h`** — the isovector term IS the skein relation\n`σ - σ⁻¹ = q - q⁻¹`. No free coefficient, and no `δ`: this is the same value\nunder every `pn_convention`, because neither `fPP` nor `fNN` mentions `δ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.fPNbringQuad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.fPNbringQuad","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L122-L124","doc":"`f_pn` under `bring_color_weighted` is `z - h(1/2 - δ/4)`; quadrupled,\n`4z - 2h + hδ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.fPNstrictQuad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.fPNstrictQuad","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L118-L121","doc":"`f_pn` under `strict_averaged` is `z - h/2`; stated **quadrupled** as\n`4z - 2h` so that nothing below needs division and the base ring stays a bare\n`CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.fNN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.fNN","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L116-L117","doc":"`f_nn = z - h` — the negative crossing, under `σ⁻¹ = σ - h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.fPP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.fPP","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L114-L115","doc":"`f_pp = z` — the positive crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.ocr_exponent_fails_at_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.ocr_exponent_fails_at_two","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L104-L107","doc":"**The `(-1)^n` reading fails at `n = 2`** whenever `g < 0`, which is the\nwhole repulsive class. Stated as the negation, since that is the use. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.ursell3_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.ursell3_pos","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L83-L102","doc":"**`φᵀ₃ > 0`** for `g ∈ (-1, 0)` — the opposite sign, and the sign nature has.\nThe proof is the regrouping `g₁₂g₁₃ + g₁₂g₁₃g₂₃ = g₁₂g₁₃(1 + g₂₃)`, in which\nevery factor is positive: two negatives multiply to a positive, and `1 + g > 0`\nis exactly `g > -1`.\n\nNote the hypotheses: all three variables must be **negative**, but only **one**\nof them needs `> -1`. The repulsive class gives `-1 < g < 0` on all three, so the\ntheorem applies; it is stated at the weaker hypothesis because that is what the\nproof uses, and a Lean file should not carry hypotheses it does not need. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.ursell2_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.ursell2_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L79-L81","doc":"**`φᵀ₂ ≤ 0`.** This is what settles the OCR'd exponent: the reading\n`(-1)^n φᵀ_n ≥ 0` would demand `φᵀ₂ ≥ 0` and fails immediately. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.corpusB3_closed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.corpusB3_closed","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L64-L67","doc":"The closed form the identity reduces to: `b₃ = f₁₂ + f₁₃ + f₂₃ - 2 - f₁₂f₁₃f₂₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.corpusB3_eq_neg_ursell3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.corpusB3_eq_neg_ursell3","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L58-L62","doc":"**`b₃ = -φᵀ₃`, exactly, for every triple.** This is the identity the probe\nsampled; it is now proved rather than tested. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.W2_eq_neg_ursell2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.W2_eq_neg_ursell2","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L54-L56","doc":"**`W(2) = -φᵀ₂`** under the Boltzmann identification `g = f - 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.ursell3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.ursell3","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L49-L52","doc":"The third Ursell function, `φᵀ₃ = Σ_{G connected on 3} ∏_{E(G)} g`: the three\ntwo-edge paths and the triangle (Jansen–Kolesnikov p. 5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.ursell2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.ursell2","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L45-L47","doc":"The second Ursell function, `φᵀ₂ = g` — the single connected graph on two\nvertices is the edge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.corpusB3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.corpusB3","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L40-L43","doc":"The corpus's connected 3-body cumulant,\n`b₃ = W(3) - [W(12) + W(13) + W(23)]` with `W(S) = 1 - ∏ f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.W2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondArcTheorems.W2","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondArcTheorems.lean#L37-L38","doc":"The corpus's multiplicative assembly on a pair: `W = 1 - f`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}